<title>FRANCE: Bouygues wins Russian space centre deal.</title>
<headline>Bouygues wins Russian space centre deal.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>French construction company Bouygues said on Tuesday it has won a contract from the Russian space research centre to build its new centrifugal simulator.</p>
<p>The contract is worth nearly 170 million francs and allows 20 months to build the simulator, which will be in the Moscow region and be used for Russian and international astronauts, Bouygues said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
